{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_012 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. Key findings: multiprofile >> singleprofile (+0.17 acc), transformer aggregation > avgpool (+0.02 acc), and weighted ≈ concat fusion (negligible difference). The RNA encoder is the major unexplored axis — we have only tested scvi_n200. Question: Does scgpt, a more expressive pretrained single-cell language model, outperform scvi_n200 when paired with the proven best architecture (multiprofile + transformer + weighted + imagenet_vit_l)? This is the highest-value exploration because the RNA encoder directly shapes the modality representation fed into fusion, and scgpt's larger pretrained capacity could capture richer gene-expression semantics. Why this is the best next experiment: It isolates a single variable (RNA encoder) while holding all other settings at their empirically best values, giving a clean comparison to config_012. Expected cost: scgpt is a large transformer-based encoder, so I estimate ~5–6 GPU hours (moderately higher than config_012's 3.60 h due to the larger RNA backbone), which is acceptable given the potential accuracy gain and the 5 remaining experiments."
}

